From: claude-bot <claude-bot@localhost>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 03:30:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] epaint: draw a cluster with more glyphs than characters
 as one bitmap
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Some fonts compose a letter from a base glyph and mark glyphs (Hack's `ǻ`,
Noto Naskh Arabic's `ب`), so one character shapes to two or more glyphs.
`layout_shaped_run` emitted one `Glyph` per shaped glyph, which broke the
`glyphs.len() == char_count` invariant the cursor and selection code rely
on: in a `TextEdit`, every such letter shifted the caret one slot.

Such a cluster is now rendered into one atlas entry, the outlines of all
its glyphs filled together at their shaped offsets, and carried by the
cluster's first character with the cluster's whole advance. The entry is
cached and sub-pixel binned like a single glyph, keyed by every glyph and
offset in it. Clusters with a `.notdef` or a color glyph keep the old
per-glyph path.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
